 "title": "Homepage | Ramsey County, Minnesota",
 "text": "Homepage | Ramsey County, Minnesota Skip to main content Language\nHome Jobs News & Updates Calendar Contact Us\nResidents Residents Overview\nAssistance & Support\nElections & Voting\nEmergency Response & Preparedness\nEnvironment\nHealth & Medical\nLibraries\nLicenses, Permits & Records\nParks & Recreation\nProperty & Home\nPublic Safety & Law\nRecycling & Waste\nRoads & Transportation\nEvent Spaces\nBusinesses Businesses Overview\nDoing Business with Ramsey County\nWorkforce & Business Development\nLicenses, Permits & Inspections\nProperty & Development\nRecycling & Waste\nTransit Sales & Use Tax\nYour Government Your Government Overview\nLeadership\nAbout Ramsey County\nContacts & Locations\nDepartments\nProjects & Initiatives\nOrdinances & Regulations\nVolunteer\nOpen Government\nRamsey County, Minnesota\nA vibrant community where all are valued and thrive.\nGet help... Pay... Apply... Find... File... Report... Vote...\nResidents\nBusinesses\nYour Government\nGeneral election is Tuesday, Nov. 3\nPrepare for Election Day by exploring your voting options and reviewing important election information. Find early voting options, check your voter registration, locate your polling place, review important election dates and get answers to frequently asked questions.\nVoting FAQ Vote before election day\nNews and updates\nSecond half of 2026 property tax payments due Oct. 15\nPayments must be postmarked on or before Oct. 15 to avoid penalty.\nOctober 8, 2026\nProperty taxes and values\nRead more\nEarly voting begins Oct. 16\nAbsentee voting remains available by mail or in person at the Plato building from Sept. 18–Oct. 15.\nOctober 1, 2026\nElections\nRead more\nTake the Save Food, Spend Less Challenge\nWhat would you do with an extra few thousand dollars? The average family of four spends about $58 a week ($3,000 a year) on food they end up throwing away. This challenge will help improve your skills in cooking, planning, shopping and storage to save time, money and resources.\nOctober 1, 2026\nEnvironmental health and recycling\nRead more\nDeer management hunts start Oct. 20\nDaylong hunts will be conducted at seven park and trail locations on select dates in October, November and December.\nSeptember 14, 2026\nParks and recreation\nRead more\nAll news and updates\nMeetings and events\nOCT 19\nIn-Person Public Charge Rule Legal Help Session\nMonday, October 19, 2026\n11:00 a.m.\nService Center - Downtown Saint Paul\nTrainings and workshops\nView event\nOCT 20\nBoard of Commissioners Meeting\nTuesday, October 20, 2026\n9:00 a.m.\nSaint Paul City Hall - Ramsey County Courthouse\nBoard of commissioners\nView event\nOCT 20\nManufacturing Employer of the Day: Westinghouse\nTuesday, October 20, 2026\n3-5 p.m.\nRamsey County Library - Roseville\nJob fairs\nView event\nAll meetings and events\nBoard meetings & information\nMeet the commissioners Board meetings and workshops\nBack to top\nConnect with Ramsey County\nA county of excellence working with you to enhance our quality of life.\nContact us Sign up for email updates\nResidents Assistance & Support Elections & Voting Emergency Response & Preparedness Environment Health & Medical Libraries Licenses, Permits & Records Parks & Recreation Property & Home Public Safety & Law Recycling & Waste Roads & Transportation Event Spaces\nBusinesses Doing Business with Ramsey County Workforce & Business Development Licenses, Permits & Inspections Property & Development Recycling & Waste Transit Sales & Use Tax\nYour Government Leadership About Ramsey County Contacts & Locations Departments Projects & Initiatives Ordinances & Regulations Volunteer Open Government\n© 2026 Ramsey County, MN. All rights reserved.\nTerms of Use\nContact Us\nFor Employees\nWeb Accessibility\nPowered by Interpersonal Frequency",
